<%
  ios = ENV["APP_STORE_URL"].presence
  android = ENV["PLAY_STORE_URL"].presence
%>
<% content_for :title, "Gloslate · Split rent, bills and groceries without the math" %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <meta name="description" content="Gloslate keeps a running tab with the people you live with, travel with, or just grab lunch with, then tells each person exactly what to send. On iPhone, Android and the web. Free. Gloslate never touches your money.">
  <link rel="canonical" href="<%= ENV.fetch('PUBLIC_URL', 'https://gloslate.app') %>/">
  <meta property="og:type" content="website">
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="Gloslate">
  <meta property="og:title" content="Gloslate · Stop texting “you owe me.”">
  <meta property="og:description" content="A running tab for your home, your trips and your friends. One number, already netted. Pay in the app you already use.">
  <meta property="og:image" content="<%= ENV.fetch('PUBLIC_URL', 'https://gloslate.app') %>/site/og-v3.png">
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
<% end %>
<% content_for :styles do %><style><%= raw File.read(Rails.root.join("app/assets/stylesheets/site.css")) %></style><% end %>

<%= render "public/site_nav" %>

<main id="main">
<div class="container">

  <section class="hero" id="get">
    <i class="fly" style="left:6%;top:12%" aria-hidden="true"></i><i class="fly" style="left:47%;top:8%;animation-delay:-3s" aria-hidden="true"></i><i class="fly" style="left:92%;top:44%;animation-delay:-5s" aria-hidden="true"></i><i class="fly" style="left:38%;top:88%;animation-delay:-1.5s" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">For roommates, friends and trips</div>
      <h1 class="display">Stop texting<br>“you owe me.”</h1>
      <p class="lede">Rent with your roommates, a weekend trip with friends, or lunch you covered for a co-worker. Gloslate keeps the tab, does the math, and tells each person exactly what to send. No spreadsheets. No calculator screenshots. No awkward reminders.</p>
      <div class="stores">
        <a class="store" href="<%= ios || '#get' %>"><%= render "public/ico", name: :phone, color: "var(--on-glow)", size: 20 %><%= ios ? "Get it on iPhone" : "Coming soon to iPhone" %></a>
        <a class="store alt" href="<%= android || '#get' %>"><%= render "public/ico", name: :phone, color: "var(--on-dark)", size: 20 %><%= android ? "Get it on Android" : "Coming soon to Android" %></a>
      </div>
      <p class="web-link">Or use it in your browser: <a href="https://app.gloslate.app">open the web app</a></p>
      <div class="small-print">
        <span><%= render "public/ico", name: :check, color: "var(--on-dark-owed)", size: 16, weight: 2.6 %>Free</span>
        <span><%= render "public/ico", name: :check, color: "var(--on-dark-owed)", size: 16, weight: 2.6 %>No ads</span>
        <span><%= render "public/ico", name: :check, color: "var(--on-dark-owed)", size: 16, weight: 2.6 %>Never touches your money</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-art">
      <div class="device back"><img src="/site/app-request-v3.webp" width="390" height="844" alt="A Gloslate payment request page showing the total, the breakdown, and a Pay button"></div>
      <div class="device front"><img src="/site/app-home-v2.webp" width="390" height="844" alt="The Gloslate home screen showing one balance, Alex owes you $909.15, with a Request button"></div>
      <div class="bubble one" aria-hidden="true"><%= render "public/ico", name: :check, color: "var(--owed)", size: 18, weight: 2.6 %>Alex paid $909.15</div>
      <div class="bubble two" aria-hidden="true"><%= render "public/ico", name: :calendar, size: 18 %>Rent posted · your half $900</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="pay-with">
    <span>Pay each other the way you already do:</span>
    <span class="chip">Venmo</span><span class="chip">Cash App</span><span class="chip">Zelle</span><span class="chip">Cash</span>
  </div>

  <section class="block center" id="how">
    <div class="eyebrow">How it works</div>
    <h2 class="h2">Log it in three taps. Gloslate does the math.</h2>
    <p class="lede">Your home, a group trip, or just you and one friend. After that, the tab keeps itself.</p>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step"><span class="num">01</span><h3>Start a tab</h3><p>Set up your home once and bills like rent post themselves. Or start a group for a trip, or settle up with just one person. Add people by name; they join with a link when they're ready.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><span class="num">02</span><h3>Add what people paid</h3><p>Groceries, a cabin, a pizza for four. Type the amount and who paid, even when two people split the bill. Everyone sees it right away, with their share already worked out.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><span class="num">03</span><h3>Settle up in the fewest payments</h3><p>One number per person, already netted. In a group, Gloslate works out the fewest payments that settle everyone. Send a request, they pay in the app they already use, and you're even.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="features">
    <div class="show">
      <div class="show-art"><div class="device"><img src="/site/app-trip-v2.webp" width="390" height="844" alt="A Gatlinburg trip in Gloslate: you're owed $215, settled in three payments from Cy, Ben and Ana"></div></div>
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">One number</div>
        <h2 class="h2">Everything nets out. Nobody does subtraction.</h2>
        <p class="lede">You covered rent, they covered dinner. Two of you split the cabin on the trip. Gloslate nets it all out and shows one amount per person, with every line behind it a tap away.</p>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li><%= render "public/ico", name: :check, color: "var(--owed)", weight: 2.6 %><div><b>Fewest payments possible.</b> <span>With three or more people, Gloslate finds the shortest way for everyone to get square.</span></div></li>
          <li><%= render "public/ico", name: :check, color: "var(--owed)", weight: 2.6 %><div><b>Any split you like.</b> <span>Even, by percentage, by exact amount, or by shares. Your usual split is saved.</span></div></li>
          <li><%= render "public/ico", name: :check, color: "var(--owed)", weight: 2.6 %><div><b>Every change is kept.</b> <span>Edits and deletions are recorded with what changed, so nothing quietly disappears.</span></div></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="show flip">
      <div class="show-art"><div class="device"><img src="/site/app-friends-v1.webp" width="390" height="844" alt="The Friends tab: Balances with Jordan and Taylor at the top, then friends who are all square, then groups"></div></div>
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Friends</div>
        <h2 class="h2">Who owes, and who's just a friend.</h2>
        <p class="lede">You don't need a shared home to use Gloslate. Add friends once with your link, then settle up one-on-one or start a group for a trip. Anyone you owe, or who owes you, sits at the top; everyone else is right below.</p>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li><%= render "public/ico", name: :check, color: "var(--owed)", weight: 2.6 %><div><b>Requests that just arrive.</b> <span>Friends on Gloslate get your request as a notification, no link to text.</span></div></li>
          <li><%= render "public/ico", name: :check, color: "var(--owed)", weight: 2.6 %><div><b>Your tone, your call.</b> <span>Requests and reminders go out Gentle, Plain or Cheeky. Always kind, never pushy.</span></div></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="show">
      <div class="show-art"><div class="device"><img src="/site/app-cleanslate-v1.webp" width="390" height="844" alt="The clean slate moment: the Gloslate bunny sits on a slate with a check and a glowing star. Clean slate with Alex."></div></div>
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">The clean slate</div>
        <h2 class="h2">Settled feels like something.</h2>
        <p class="lede">When you confirm the payment that squares you up, the bunny hops onto the slate, wipes it clean and the star lights up. Clean slate with Alex. Pick full screen, a card or a bottom sheet in Settings.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="show flip">
      <div class="show-art"><div class="device"><img src="/site/app-bills-v2.webp" width="390" height="844" alt="Bills screen listing rent, electric and water, with the electric amount waiting to be entered"></div></div>
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Recurring bills</div>
        <h2 class="h2">Bills that post themselves.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Rent goes on the tab on the 1st. When the electric bill arrives, whoever pays it types the amount once and Gloslate splits it for everyone.</p>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li><%= render "public/ico", name: :check, color: "var(--owed)", weight: 2.6 %><div><b>Moving in or out mid-month?</b> <span>Bills split by the days each person actually lived there.</span></div></li>
          <li><%= render "public/ico", name: :check, color: "var(--owed)", weight: 2.6 %><div><b>A gentle nudge</b> <span>if a bill's amount is still missing a few days after it usually arrives.</span></div></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="show">
      <div class="show-art"><div class="device"><img src="/site/app-request-v3.webp" width="390" height="844" alt="A payment request page with Venmo and Cash App buttons"></div></div>
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Payment requests</div>
        <h2 class="h2">A link instead of a lecture.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Every request is a clean page with the total, the breakdown and a Pay button that opens Venmo or Cash App with the amount filled in. It works on any phone, even if they never download Gloslate.</p>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li><%= render "public/ico", name: :check, color: "var(--owed)", weight: 2.6 %><div><b>Nudges, not nagging.</b> <span>Set a limit like $40 or 7 days and Gloslate sends the reminder, so nobody has to be the bad guy.</span></div></li>
          <li><%= render "public/ico", name: :check, color: "var(--owed)", weight: 2.6 %><div><b>Paid means paid.</b> <span>One person marks it, the other confirms it arrived, and it's off the list for good.</span></div></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="show flip">
      <div class="show-art"><div class="device"><img src="/site/app-statement-v2.webp" width="390" height="844" alt="An October statement: Alex sends you $475.67, with the month's totals and items"></div></div>
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Monthly statements</div>
        <h2 class="h2">A clean record of every month.</h2>
        <p class="lede">On your statement day Gloslate closes the month: what you spent together, who paid what, and exactly what clears it. Download it as a PDF for a move-out, a landlord or taxes.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block center">
    <div class="eyebrow">And the little things</div>
    <h2 class="h2">Built for real life.</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="tile"><div class="ico"><%= render "public/ico", name: :scan %></div><h3>Scan a receipt</h3><p>Point your camera at a receipt and the total fills itself in. The text is read on your phone, not on our servers.</p></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="ico"><%= render "public/ico", name: :split %></div><h3>Who had what</h3><p>Tap who had each item on a dinner bill. Tax and tip split in proportion, down to the cent.</p></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="ico"><%= render "public/ico", name: :people %></div><h3>One friend or twenty</h3><p>Your home with up to 5 people, a trip with up to 20, or a one-on-one tab with a friend. Choose who's in on each expense.</p></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="ico"><%= render "public/ico", name: :widget %></div><h3>Home screen widget</h3><p>Your balance at a glance on your home screen, on iPhone and Android.</p></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="ico"><%= render "public/ico", name: :lock %></div><h3>Face ID lock</h3><p>Keep your balances to yourself with Face ID or your passcode.</p></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="ico"><%= render "public/ico", name: :tablet %></div><h3>Phone, tablet, foldable</h3><p>Designed for iPhone, iPad and Android phones, tablets and foldables.</p></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="ico"><%= render "public/ico", name: :bell %></div><h3>Quiet hours</h3><p>Notifications wait until morning, and you choose which ones you get.</p></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="ico"><%= render "public/ico", name: :download %></div><h3>Your data, anytime</h3><p>Export a year as a spreadsheet, or everything about you as a file.</p></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="ico"><%= render "public/ico", name: :link %></div><h3>Invite with a link</h3><p>Add people before they join. When they do, everything is already there.</p></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="ico"><%= render "public/ico", name: :browser %></div><h3>Works in your browser</h3><p>Use Gloslate on any computer at app.gloslate.app, with the same account as your phone.</p></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="ico"><%= render "public/ico", name: :chat %></div><h3>Sign in with Glofly</h3><p>Already on Glofly? Sign in with one tap, alongside Apple, Google, email or your phone number.</p></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="ico"><%= render "public/ico", name: :sparkle %></div><h3>Reminders in your tone</h3><p>Gentle, Plain or Cheeky. Gloslate does the nudging so you don't have to.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" id="privacy">
    <div class="trust">
      <div class="eyebrow">Privacy and trust</div>
      <h2 class="h2">Your money stays yours.</h2>
      <div class="trust-grid">
        <div><%= render "public/ico", name: :shield, color: "var(--on-dark-owed)", size: 28 %><h3>We never touch your money</h3><p>Gloslate tracks who owes what and opens the payment app you already use. No bank logins, no card numbers, no money passing through us.</p></div>
        <div><%= render "public/ico", name: :receipt, color: "var(--on-dark-owed)", size: 28 %><h3>Receipts read on your phone</h3><p>Receipt scanning happens on your device. A photo is only uploaded if you choose to attach it.</p></div>
        <div><%= render "public/ico", name: :trash, color: "var(--on-dark-owed)", size: 28 %><h3>Leave whenever you want</h3><p>Export your data or delete your account from Settings. No ads, and we don't sell your information.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin:28px 0 0"><a href="/privacy" style="color:var(--on-dark);font-weight:700">Read the privacy policy →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="pricing">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Pricing</div>
        <h2 class="h2">Free for your home, your trips and your friends.</h2>
        <p class="muted" style="line-height:1.6;margin:0">Unlimited expenses, every day. No ads between screens. No caps that show up right when you need them.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="price">$0</div>
        <ul style="margin-top:20px">
          <li><%= render "public/ico", name: :check, color: "var(--owed)", weight: 2.6 %>Unlimited expenses and bills</li>
          <li><%= render "public/ico", name: :check, color: "var(--owed)", weight: 2.6 %>Payment requests and reminders</li>
          <li><%= render "public/ico", name: :check, color: "var(--owed)", weight: 2.6 %>Monthly statements and exports</li>
          <li><%= render "public/ico", name: :check, color: "var(--owed)", weight: 2.6 %>Up to 5 people per home, 20 per group</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" id="faq">
    <div class="center"><div class="eyebrow">Questions</div><h2 class="h2">Good to know</h2></div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details><summary>Does Gloslate move my money?</summary><p>No. Gloslate keeps the tab and opens Venmo or Cash App with the amount filled in, or shows the Zelle details to use. Your money never passes through Gloslate, and Gloslate never asks for your bank or card details.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Does everyone need the app?</summary><p>Not to pay you. Requests open as a web page on any phone. You can add people before they join, and everything you've logged shows up for them when they do.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can I use it for a trip or just one friend?</summary><p>Yes. Start a group for a trip or anything a few people share: everyone adds what they paid, even when two people paid for the same thing, and Gloslate works out the fewest payments to settle everyone. For one person, tap Settle up with someone, enter the amount, and send them a request.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do I need to live with someone to use it?</summary><p>No. Pick "Just with friends" when you start: add friends, settle up one-on-one, or start a group. You can set up a home any time later.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What if we don't split everything 50/50?</summary><p>Split evenly, by percentage, by exact amounts or by shares, and choose who's in on each expense. For a dinner bill, tap who had each item and Gloslate splits tax and tip in proportion.</p></details>
      <details><summary>How do bills that change every month work?</summary><p>Fixed bills like rent post themselves on the day they're due. For bills that change, like electric, Gloslate asks whoever pays it to type the amount when it arrives, then splits it for everyone.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What if someone says they paid but didn't?</summary><p>A payment only counts once the person who received it confirms it. If something looks wrong, either of you can question a payment for 30 days.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What happens when someone moves out?</summary><p>Bills split by the days each person lived there. Settle up before they go, and the history stays on everyone's statements.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Is my information private?</summary><p>Only the people in your home, tab or group see your shared expenses. Request links show first names and amounts only. We don't show ads or sell your data. <a href="/privacy">Read the privacy policy.</a></p></details>
      <details><summary>Does it work on iPad, Android and computers?</summary><p>Yes: iPhone, iPad, Android phones, tablets and foldables, and any computer's browser at <a href="https://app.gloslate.app">app.gloslate.app</a>.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can I sign in with Glofly?</summary><p>Yes. Sign in with Glofly, Apple, Google, your email or your phone number, and add more ways later in Settings. Gloslate only receives what you approve on Glofly's screen.</p></details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="final">
      <h2 class="h2">Make money the easy part.</h2>
      <p>Set up your home, start a trip, or send a friend a request in under a minute. Everyone else joins with a link.</p>
      <div class="stores">
        <a class="store" href="<%= ios || '#get' %>"><%= render "public/ico", name: :phone, color: "var(--on-glow)", size: 20 %><%= ios ? "Get it on iPhone" : "Coming soon to iPhone" %></a>
        <a class="store alt" href="<%= android || '#get' %>"><%= render "public/ico", name: :phone, color: "var(--on-dark)", size: 20 %><%= android ? "Get it on Android" : "Coming soon to Android" %></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="eyebrow">More from the creators of Gloslate</div>
    <h2 class="h2">Apps for the people you live, eat and talk with.</h2>
    <div class="family">
      <div><b>Glofly</b><p>Chat, call and hang out with your friends, on your phone, your computer or the web.</p></div>
      <div><b>Tablespin</b><p>Every dinner is a fork in the road. Spin for a pick or vote with friends on where to eat.</p></div>
      <div><b>petal</b><p>A brighter place for your people. Friends, photos and messages, with your feed in order and no ads.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>
</main>

<%= render "public/site_footer" %>
